-- =============================================================================
-- V3 - Seed data.
--
-- Generated deterministically: fixed UUIDv5 namespace, fixed RNG seeds and fixed
-- literal timestamps. There is no random() and no now() anywhere in this file, so
-- a rebuilt database is byte-for-byte the database the demo was recorded against.
--
-- Activity window: 2026-05-31 .. 2026-08-28 (90 days). Time of day follows a
-- realistic diurnal profile - card spend peaks over lunch and in the evening,
-- payments sit in business hours, crypto runs round the clock - so 'hour_of_day'
-- and the 24h aggregate windows see a plausible spread rather than a flat band.
-- 'amount' is always the settled value in the transaction currency; crypto rows
-- carry the fiat-equivalent notional (or the token count for 1:1 stablecoins), so
-- monetary thresholds are comparable across all three activity types.
--
-- PLANTED RISK PATTERNS (the demo is only useful if risk is actually findable):
--   * Marcus Holloway (US) - structuring - repeated payments just under the 10,000 reporting threshold
--   * Viktor Semenov (CY) - high-value SWIFT wires to sanctioned-jurisdiction beneficiary banks
--   * Yuki Tanaka (JP) - heavy crypto exposure to privacy chains and OFAC-listed mixers, unattributed
--   * Amara Okafor (NG) - burst of card declines followed by a large card-not-present success
--   * Ricci and Weber sit in the middle band; O'Connor, Lindqvist, Moreno,
--     Sharma, Dubois and Brunner are ordinary, so LOW/MEDIUM outcomes are reachable.
-- =============================================================================

